{"text": "Objective\n\nExperience\n\nMilitary\nExperience\n\nJohn Rounsaville\n\nFormer State Director for USDA Rural Development (Mississippi) with economic\ndevelopment, infrastructure, legal, military, and local/state/federal government\nexperience desires appointment to State Director of USDA Rural Development\n(Mississippi) in service to the Trump Administration.\n\nVice President, Strategic Services\nWaggoner Engineering, Inc., Jackson, MS\n2008 - Present\n\nPerform business development, government relations, project management, and client\nmanagement functions for regional civil engineering and planning firm. Develop project\nconcepts, proposals, strategic plans, budgets, and policy and funding strategies to\nsupport public infrastructure and economic development initiatives for local government\nand state agency clients in Mississippi, Alabama, Louisiana, and Tennessee.\n\nState Director\nUSDA Rural Development, Jackson, MS\n2006 - 2007\n\nWorked with municipal, county, state, and federal officials in the management and\nadministration of USDA Rural Development programs for the State of Mississippi during\nthe Administration of President George W. Bush. Responsible for supervising 206\nemployees and 30 local offices.\n\nPolicy Advisor\nGovernor Haley Barbour, Jackson, MS\n2004 - 2006\n\nManaged economic development, transportation, agriculture, military, environment,\nworkforce development, and energy policy portfolios on behalf of the Governor.\nWorked extensively with state agency directors, legislators, and the Mississippi\nCongressional Delegation to advance the Governor's policy agenda. Performed key\nfunctions in post-Hurricane Katrina recovery and redevelopment efforts with primary\nfocus on public infrastructure development and environmental restoration.\n\nDeputy Chief of Staff/Legislative Director/Legislative Assistant\nRepresentative Charles W. \u201cChip\u201d Pickering, Washington, DC\n1998 - 2003\n\nManaged legislative and appropriations portfolios, with primary responsibilities for\neconomic development, infrastructure, agriculture, natural resources, energy, and\nmilitary issues for the Third Congressional District of Mississippi. Supervised office staff, the\nCongressman\u2019s schedule, and media relations.\n\nDeputy Staff Judge Advocate\n\n186\" Air Refueling Wing, Key Field, Mississippi Air National Guard, Meridian, MS\n2013 - Present\nServe as chief of military justice and chief of legal assistance for the Wing. Provide legal\n\nadvice and guidance to support commanders and base operations, including the\nprovision of legal services to 1,100 Airmen assigned to the installation. Provide legal",
